		<DeletedComponentTemplates />
		<Id>265</Id>
		<Name>Thermal Control Suite</Name>
		<IsMockTemplate>false</IsMockTemplate>
		<Description>Reads the "Thermal Control" custom performance counter category registered by Thermal Control Suite (ThermalPerformanceCounters.cs, github.com/trooperthorn/thermal-control-suite) — smoothed CPU temperature, actual fan percentage, 1-minute and 5-minute trailing averages of both, and the control loop's own poll interval. Every value is a RawFraction/RawBase pair (denominator fixed at 10,000, numerator value*100) so SAM reads the cooked value directly with no scaling needed. SingleInstance category, so Instance is left blank on every component.

Prerequisites: Thermal Control Suite installed and running on the target Windows host, which registers the category at first run (or via its installer). No listening socket is opened by the app for this data; SAM reads the OS perf-counter shared memory the same way perfmon.exe or Get-Counter would.

Credentials: whatever credential the node already polls with for Windows Performance Counters (WMI or SNMP-agent based, per PreferredPollingMethod).</Description>
		<Tags>
			<TagInfo>
				<Name>Windows</Name>
				<TemplateID>265</TemplateID>
			</TagInfo>
